    "body": "**Judgement calls for the maintainer** (gate green; no posted G-code changes, because the post scripts receive no linear travel numbers):\n1. **The fix restates the two machine files; the limit check itself is unchanged.** `vmc.mch` and `tilthead.mch` now give each slide as `-L..L`, the convention the Tormach files already use and that `app::machine` documents: limits are read in program coordinates, and the file can't know where the work offset sits. The other choice was an absolute check in the machine frame. That needs a new `.mch` key and a setup setting for where the work offset sits in machine coordinates, so it's left to an enhancement (see `docs/decisions/457-vmc-z-stroke.md`).\n2. **The same flaw likely remains in two files I didn't touch:** `lathe.mch` and `millturn.mch` keep a one-sided Z band. Filed separately (linked below).",
